<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khwarazm</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khwarazm is a historical region around the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> river and its delta south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aral-sea">Aral Sea</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a> and Turkmenistan. An ancient centre of irrigated agriculture and trade, it gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a>, whose shahs built a large state from this base in the twelfth and early thirteenth centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khwarazm.jpg" alt="Khwarazm" width="320" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HistoryofIran · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Khwarazm_in_the_Islamic_period,_before_the_Mongol_invasion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
